{"id":"n-20261016-s44lkx","category":"finance","display_title":"Housing and Inflation Trends","display_title_he":"מגמות דיור ואינפלציה","short_summary":"Recent data from the Central Bureau of Statistics reveals a monthly drop in the Consumer Price Index and property prices alongside rising rental costs for new tenants.","english_level":"C1","words":542,"reading_time":4,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/UK_CPI_and_CPIH_inflation_since_1950.png/960px-UK_CPI_and_CPIH_inflation_since_1950.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Firebrace · CC BY 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UK_CPI_and_CPIH_inflation_since_1950.png"},"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3872387","title":"שוק הדיור רותח: הנתון שלא ראינו 10 שנים - והניגוד הבלתי נתפס בשכירות","published_at":"2026-10-15T18:30:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-15T18:30:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-16T05:55:05.237Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Recent economic data released by the Central Bureau of Statistics shows that the Consumer Price Index for September recorded a decrease of 0.5 percent compared to the month of August. Despite this monthly decline, the annual inflation rate edged up slightly to 1.6 percent, compared to 1.5 percent in the previous month, remaining within the official target range of up to 3 percent.","The September report highlighted distinct shifts across various consumer sectors. Notable price decreases were observed in culture and entertainment, which dropped by 2.7 percent, transportation, which fell by 2.5 percent, and clothing and footwear, which decreased by 0.9 percent. General food items as well as furniture and household equipment also registered declines of 0.4 percent each. Conversely, significant price increases occurred in fresh vegetables, which surged by 6.6 percent, education services, which rose by 0.8 percent, and housing rent, which went up by 0.4 percent.","A closer examination of the rental market reveals a stark contrast between existing occupants and new renters. Tenants who renewed their current contracts faced an average increase of 2.4 percent. In contrast, new renters navigating apartment turnover in sampled apartments experienced a sharp surge of 5.3 percent. These change rates reflect an approximation of the annual change in rent within these groups. Experts note that rental rates remain static for the vast majority of tenants throughout the year because they are bound by lease contracts where monthly rent is determined without indexation mechanisms.","Simultaneously, the broader housing market data presented by the Bureau indicates a continuing downward trend in property values. Comparing transactions executed between July and August against the preceding two-month period of June and July, the general apartment price index—which includes both new and second-hand apartments with quality adjustment—fell by a monthly rate of 0.6 percent. On an annual basis, comparing the current period to the same period last year, this represents a cumulative decrease of 1.8 percent. This figure establishes the current timeframe as the longest annual wave of price reductions seen over the past decade, following shorter downward segments recorded in 2018 and the second half of 2023.","New apartments mirrored this trajectory, posting monthly and annual declines of 0.4 percent. When government-subsidized transactions, which expanded to account for 45.8 percent of all deals, are factored out, the drop in the free market deepens to 0.8 percent. Nevertheless, viewed over a five-year perspective since July and August 2021, new apartment prices still present a sharp cumulative increase of 24.3 percent, compared to a surge of 26.8 percent across all property prices overall.","Geographical analysis categorized by administrative districts indicates that this negative trend encompasses the entire country, with annual price decreases registered in every single district. The Central district experienced the sharpest annual drop with a plunge of 2.7 percent, followed closely by Tel Aviv with a decrease of 1.9 percent. The Southern district registered a drop of 1.5 percent, Haifa saw 1.4 percent, the North recorded 0.8 percent, and the Jerusalem area experienced a moderate easing of 0.2 percent. On a monthly comparison examining July and August versus June and July, most areas continued to exhibit weakness, led by the Northern district which recorded a drop of 1.5 percent, Tel Aviv at 0.9 percent, the Center at 0.7 percent, Jerusalem at 0.3 percent, and the South at 0.1 percent. The sole district that recorded a slight monthly increase against the national trend was Haifa, which registered a minor rise of 0.4 percent."],"facts":[{"fact":"The Consumer Price Index (CPI) for September 2026 recorded a decrease of 0.5% compared to August 2026, according to the Central Bureau of Statistics.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Annual inflation rose slightly to 1.6%, remaining within the target range of up to 3%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Notable price decreases in September were seen in culture and entertainment (-2.7%), transportation (-2.5%), and clothing and footwear (-0.9%).","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Price increases in September were led by fresh vegetables (+6.6%), education services (+0.8%), and rent (+0.4%).","sources":[1]},{"fact":"For tenants renewing an existing contract, rent increased by 2.4%, whereas new tenants facing tenant turnover experienced a 5.3% surge.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The overall property price index, covering new and second-hand apartments, fell by 0.6% between July-August and June-July 2026.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Annually, property prices dropped by 1.8%, marking the longest annual price decline wave in the past decade.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"New apartment prices dropped 0.4% monthly and annually, with government-subsidized transactions expanding to 45.8% of all deals.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Over a five-year perspective since 2021, new apartment prices show a cumulative increase of 24.3%, compared to a 26.8% surge in overall property prices.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Annual property price drops affected all districts, led by the Central district (-2.7%) and Tel Aviv (-1.9%).","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Recent","lemma":"recent","pos":"adj","he":"אחרון","name":"recent"},{"text":"economic","lemma":"economic","pos":"adj","he":"כלכלי","name":false},{"text":"data","lemma":"data","pos":"n","he":"נתונים","name":false},{"text":"released","lemma":"release","pos":"v","he":"פורסם","name":false},{"text":"by","lemma":"by","pos":"prep","he":"על ידי","name":false},{"text":"the","lemma":"the","pos":"det","he":"ה-","name":false},{"text":"Central Bureau of Statistics","lemma":"Central Bureau of Statistics","pos":"n","he":"הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה","name":"Central Bureau of Statistics"},{"text":"shows","lemma":"show","pos":"v","he":"מראה","name":false},{"text":"that","lemma":"that","pos":"conj","he":"כי","name":false},{"text":"Consumer Price Index","lemma":"Consumer Price Index","pos":"n","he":"מדד המחירים לצרכן","name":"Consumer Price Index"},{"text":"for","lemma":"for","pos":"prep","he":"עבור","name":false},{"text":"September","lemma":"September","pos":"n","he":"ספטמבר","name":"September"},{"text":"recorded","lemma":"record","pos":"v","he":"רשם","name":false},{"text":"a","lemma":"a","pos":"det","he":"ה-","name":false},{"text":"decrease","lemma":"decrease","pos":"n","he":"ירידה","name":false},{"text":"of","lemma":"of","pos":"prep","he":"של","name":false},{"text":"0.5 percent","lemma":"0.5 percent","pos":"n","he":"0.5 אחוז","name":"0.5 percent"},{"text":"compared","lemma":"compare","pos":"v","he":"בהשוואה","name":false},{"text":"to","lemma":"to","pos":"prep","he":"אל","name":false},{"text":"month","lemma":"mo